.TH FSCK_EXT2FS 8
.SH NAME
fsck_ext2fs \- check a supported ext2 filesystem
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fsck_ext2fs
[\-n|\-y|\-p] [\-f] [\-v] special
.SH DESCRIPTION
Invokes /sbin/e2fsck directly. With no repair option, e2fsck prompts as usual.
Repair modes are mutually exclusive. Mounted targets and failed mount-table
or device inspection are refused, including read-only checks.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Preserves e2fsck's bitmask: 0 clean, 1 corrected, 2 reboot advised,
4 errors remain, 8 operational failure, 16 usage, 32 cancelled,
128 library error. Bits may be combined. Child signals and fork, exec,
or wait failures return 8.
.SH SEE ALSO
newfs_ext2fs(8), e2fsck(8)
